# Frontend Conventions

## Template structure
```
templates/
  base.html              ← loads tokens.css + gov-style.css, Lottie, HTMX
                           GOI DBIM Header 1: tricolor → a11y bar → gov-header → gov-navbar
  core/home.html         ← hero with Ashoka Chakra + 6 GOI-card service grid
  chat/chat.html         ← chat bubble partials (chat-bubble--user / --bot classes)
  wizard/step.html
partials/
  _answer.html           ← HTMX swap target
  _source_drawer.html
  _busy.html
  _error.html
static/
  css/
    tokens.css           ← GOI DBIM-aligned color tokens (--color-primary, --gov-saffron, etc.)
    gov-style.css        ← GOI components (tricolor, a11y bar, header, navbar, cards, buttons)
  images/
    ashoka-chakra.svg    ← 24-spoke Dharma Wheel (decorative hero element)
    national-emblem.svg  ← Placeholder; replace with official from india.gov.in before submission
```

## HTMX patterns
- Swap target: `hx-target="#answer-area"` with `hx-swap="innerHTML"`
- Show loading: `hx-indicator="#thinking-dots"` (CSS class `htmx-request`)
- Cancel button: `hx-delete="/assistant/cancel/" hx-vals='{"request_id":"..."}'`
- No Alpine.js; use vanilla JS for any interactivity beyond HTMX

## CSS design system
- Import `{% static 'css/tokens.css' %}` AND `{% static 'css/gov-style.css' %}` in base.html
- All colors via CSS custom properties (`var(--color-primary)`, `var(--gov-saffron)`, `var(--gov-green)`)
- Never hardcode hex in templates or component styles
- 4px base grid; spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64px
- GOI component classes: `.gov-card`, `.gov-btn-primary`, `.gov-btn-secondary`, `.gov-section-title`, `.ev-label`
- GOI tricolor stripe always at top of page (`.gov-tricolor-bar`)
- Theme is opt-in: `html[data-theme="dark"]` + `#theme-toggle`. Never `prefers-color-scheme`.
- Header/footer use `--color-chrome` (stays navy). Page surfaces use `--color-bg` / `--color-surface`.
- Subtle card hover shadow via `--shadow-card-hover` — not decorative drop-shadows elsewhere

## Animation rules
- Loading state: `#thinking-dots` uses CSS keyframe `bounce-dots`
- Lottie animations via `<dotlottie-player>` web component (self-hosted CDN)
- Decorative animations must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`:
  ```css
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .lottie-anim, .animate { display: none; } }
  ```
- GSAP used only for the page-enter reveal (single tween, < 0.4s)
- No animation on data or error states

## RTL support
- Urdu, Sindhi, Kashmiri (Perso-Arabic) → `<article dir="rtl" lang="ur">`
- Source citation blocks always `dir="ltr"` (section numbers must not mirror)
- Test RTL in Chrome DevTools "Emulation → Document direction"

## Accessibility
- Every interactive element has `aria-label` or visible text label
- Focus visible outline: `outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 2px`
- Screen reader: evidence label in `role="status"` live region
- Keyboard: wizard step-through must work with Tab/Enter/Space alone
